 "spec_id": "var-gs_vy-gvy2s-v1",
 "title": "GS21 gvy25s's SIGNED type ladder over the TWO priced chains (total price 2.5, 2.5/sqrt(2) each), exposure in CASH FLOWS only: twelve hidden types = six mirrored alignments (+-1, +-0.6, +-0.2) x magnitudes 0.05, 0.10, level-compensated, 5 x 5 nodes",
 "question": "Does spreading GS21's hidden mean-zero cash-flow loading over two priced states raise room and the fair gap above gvy25s's (K = 1), as the reduced-form latent ladder did and as vym3s / vym6s test in KP14?",
 "notes": "WHY (2026-10-27). The GS21 member of the signed K ladder (KP14: vyg25s -> vym3s -> vym6s). The exposure is the KP14 one -- a type's cash flows are multiplied by exp(b_f . y) and nothing else moves with y (gs_bzl 1; the cost, coupon, investment and recovery knobs at zero) -- so the equity claim's loading is the hidden type times the firm's own leverage, as in vyg25s / bvychs. Alignments mirrored, E[b_f . gamma] = 0, hidden at y = 0 by the level compensation derived from both chains. GS21 supports two chains at most (joint Tauchen nodes), so K = 2 is the GS21 point of the ladder; the five-node chains are gvypk2's resolution (the 9 x 9 solve needs 12+ GB).\n\nFEASIBILITY: the solver accepts negative gs_bv / gs_bv2 (gvy25s: gs_ashift derived at either sign); gs_sim_vy parses GS_VY_BV2 and checks each solution's gs_bv2; the panel exports y_stand AND y2_stand (both chains) to the random features, unlike KP14's state-1-only rf_stand -- note in the report.\n\nPRECOMMITMENT STATUS: precommitted=false; ids filled from the Quest build log by the solve script before any seed runs.\n\nPREDICTION (2026-10-27): room at least gvy25s's (predicted 15-30% of the linear ceiling); fair gap +0.02 to +0.08, 8+ of 10 seeds positive. FALSIFIED as 'K raises GS21's gap' if the gap is below gvy25s's.",
 "lineage": {
  "parent_spec": "var-gs_vy-gvy25s-v1",
  "changes": [
   "six level-exposure types on one chain -> twelve types with 2-vectors (gs_bv, gs_bv2): mirrored alignments +-1, +-0.6, +-0.2 x magnitudes 0.05, 0.10",
   "second priced chain: NY2 5, gamma_v2 = gamma_v = 2.5/sqrt(2), kappa_y2 0.35; NY 9 -> 5",
   "bv_comp 1.2, kappa_y 0.35, y_mult 2.5 unchanged; twelve solves sol_gvy2sa..l"
  ]
 },
